We say it from the rostrum: the deputy prime minister has asked private men to
take up a policing function against a protest, and there is a word for a
governing party that does that. The movement hears a party willing to name what
it is facing.

The confrontation escalates on schedule. Church attendance becomes a political
uniform, our own Catholic voters in the counties hear a party at war with their
parish, and the men outside the doors acquire the recognition they came for.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

