The network we funded in the autumn already knows how to do this: marked
observers, cameras held openly, a lawyer on call, a reporting form that a court
will accept. Nobody from our party stands in a doorway shouting.

Within a fortnight the men outside the churches are the ones being documented,
and three of the incidents become prosecutions rather than competing videos.
The movement keeps its own name on the work, which is why it works.

