    (Number(Q.konf_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.15;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left defends the rule-of-law mechanism against its own government";
!}

We say plainly that money raised in common should not fund the dismantling of
courts, and that a member state which dislikes the condition is free to meet
it. It is the position we would hold in any country, including one we governed.

PiS receives the gift it wanted: an opposition party defending Brussels'
conditions against Poland's payments, quotable in every rural hall until 2023.
Konfederacja receives a smaller and more useful gift, which is proof that the
whole political class prefers the Union to the country.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@euveto_hospitals
title: Cost the veto in hospitals, rail and local budgets
subtitle: Refuses the sovereignty frame by refusing to discuss it; the courts argument is left to somebody else.
on-arrival: {!
