    0, (Number(Q.judicial_legitimacy) || 0) - 2
);
Q.news_headline =
    "The veto is priced in hospital wings, rail lines and county budgets";
!}

We refuse to have the argument they want. Instead we publish what the blocked
money was going to build, district by district: the hospital wing, the water
treatment plant, the rail branch, the thermal upgrade for a school.

It travels, including to people who have never cared what a disciplinary
chamber is. The concession is that we have implicitly agreed the courts are a
side issue — which is exactly how the government would like the next three
years to be discussed.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@euveto_sovereignty
title: Attack the veto as a bluff that will collapse and cost us the seat at the table
subtitle: Predicts the retreat before it happens; if the government wins a face-saving formula we look like we were rooting for Brussels.
