Q.left_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left predicts the veto will fold into a face-saving declaration";
!}

Our foreign-affairs people say what the finance ministry says in private: the
Union can build the fund outside the treaty framework, Warsaw knows it, and
this ends in a declaration that changes nothing and is presented at home as a
triumph.

The prediction is correct within weeks, which is satisfying and politically
awkward. Having spent December explaining that our government's threat was
hollow, we spend January explaining why we are not pleased about it.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@euveto_gowin
title: Offer Gowin's wing a parliamentary guarantee against the veto
subtitle: Requires a visibly fractured United Right. Splits the governing camp on Europe a year before it splits on anything else.
choose-if: united_right_cohesion <= 45
unavailable-subtitle: The United Right is still holding together — no wing of it needs an opposition guarantee to survive a vote.
