Q.razem_dissent = (Number(Q.razem_dissent) || 0) + 4;
Q.news_headline =
    "Opposition votes are offered to the governing wing that opposes the veto";
!}

The offer is made quietly and in writing: if Gowin's deputies will not carry
the veto, our votes exist to make sure the government's European position
survives without them. It is not a coalition and nobody signs anything.

It is the first working channel between our caucus and a wing of the governing
camp, and it is the reason that wing survives long enough to leave on its own
terms later. Razem asks, reasonably, at what point a channel becomes a
relationship.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

